think session-output/ seated: gitignored, one per-seat file, overwritten in place, teed by each loop's outer wrapper -- a read window beside the loops/ state room, in .gitignore, the card, and both read-scope twins. Mind's clone brought current and its stale %295 gate cleared; its stash holds a real unlanded reconnect patch with its own review recipe, left intact and named on the card.
obs On Mind versus Dream: Mind's custody file is all-stop -- any recorded gate opens the circuit and kills the loop -- while Dream's shape parks a gated question and keeps rolling to the next admissible crux. For true custody the stop is right; for a design question it turns one closed door into a dead engine, and tonight's gate was a question already answered upstream. The molt worth wording: split CUSTODY (hard gates, stop) from PARKED (design questions written down, lap picks another crux, stop only when no admissible crux remains) -- a user-owned signed change to Mind's prompt and supervisor, proposed and awaiting the word.
